# /etc/fstab - filesystems /etc/rc mounts at boot with `mount -a`
# (shell completeness S6; docs/userland/design.md, "Mounting").
#
# device      directory  type     options   dump  pass
#
# The root is not listed: init mounts it from the command line's root=.
# A device is /dev/NAME as lsblk names it; LABEL= and UUID= are not
# understood (blkid prints both). The types are cosmofs, ramfs and proc;
# the one option is ro (or rw, defaults). For example:
#
# /dev/vdb    /data      cosmofs  defaults  0     0
